# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository and on checkout, on every
# platform. Two reasons.
#
# The runtime is Linux containers: a shell script or entrypoint carrying CRLF fails
# there with an obscure "bad interpreter" error that costs an afternoon to diagnose.
#
# And this working tree is read by more than one git. A Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true writes CRLF, which tooling configured for LF then reports as every
# line changed — making `git status` useless for telling a real change from noise.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never convert binaries. None are tracked yet; these guard the screenshots and fonts
# that arrive with the README in S10.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
